# The rules of this project. The team owns this file: edit a rule to tune it, set level off
# to turn it off, or delete it. What the check enforces is what this file says.
# The draft of defaults v1. It is not frozen (plan-r3, section 4).

# A plain leaf does not import `net/http`, `net`, `database/sql`, or `os/exec`, even for a type.
rule ARCH-01
  kind depends
  level error
  from leaf
  packages net/http net database/sql os/exec
  reason Inner code must not know the web or the database.
  source Robert C. Martin, The Clean Architecture (https://blog.cleancoder.com/uncle-bob/2012/08/13/the-clean-architecture.html); Alistair Cockburn, Hexagonal Architecture (https://alistair.cockburn.us/hexagonal-architecture/)

# A library does not import `net/http` or `database/sql`.
rule ARCH-02
  kind depends
  level error
  from library
  packages net/http database/sql
  reason A shared library that knows transport or storage spreads that knowledge to each leaf.
  source Robert C. Martin, The Clean Architecture (https://blog.cleancoder.com/uncle-bob/2012/08/13/the-clean-architecture.html); Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md)

# A port signature does not carry `*http.Request`, `http.ResponseWriter`, `*http.Response`, `*sql.DB`, `*sql.Tx`, `*sql.Rows`, or `net.Conn`.
rule ARCH-03
  kind declaration
  level error
  at port-signature
  deny-types *net/http.Request net/http.ResponseWriter *net/http.Response *database/sql.DB *database/sql.Tx *database/sql.Rows net.Conn
  reason Only simple data crosses a boundary, so a consumer stays free of provider details.
  source Robert C. Martin, The Clean Architecture (https://blog.cleancoder.com/uncle-bob/2012/08/13/the-clean-architecture.html); Microsoft Azure Architecture Center, Anti-Corruption Layer pattern (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/patterns/anti-corruption-layer)

# Each entry in `strict_exempt`, `strict_interfaces`, `strict_shared`, `allow_network`, and `allow_acquiring` has a comment that gives the reason.
rule ARCH-06
  kind declaration
  level error
  at config-entry
  require comment
  reason A reviewer must see why a guard is off.
  source Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md); golangci-lint, Linters (https://golangci-lint.run/docs/linters/)

# Code in a leaf uses another leaf only through a port, a topic, or a library.
rule ARCH-07
  kind depends
  level error
  from leaf gateway entry
  deny leaf gateway entry
  via import
  reason Declared boundaries are the base of each other architecture rule.
  source Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md); Alistair Cockburn, Hexagonal Architecture (https://alistair.cockburn.us/hexagonal-architecture/)

# Only a gateway leaf or an entry leaf reaches a network function.
rule ARCH-10
  kind only-in
  level error
  effect network
  in gateway entry
  reason A reviewer finds all traffic in known places.
  source Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md); Alistair Cockburn, Hexagonal Architecture (https://alistair.cockburn.us/hexagonal-architecture/)

# An entry leaf reaches only serve functions, and only a gateway leaf reaches a dial function.
rule ARCH-11
  kind only-in
  level error
  effect dial
  in gateway
  reason A leaf that both serves and dials hides an outbound path from the diagram.
  source Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md)

# Leaf code and library code do not call a global mutator such as `os.Setenv`, `http.Handle`, `slog.SetDefault`, or `flag.Parse`.
rule ARCH-19
  kind forbid-call
  level error
  funcs os.Setenv os.Unsetenv os.Clearenv os.Chdir net/http.Handle net/http.HandleFunc expvar.Publish expvar.NewInt expvar.NewFloat expvar.NewMap expvar.NewString flag.Parse flag.Set flag.String flag.Int flag.Int64 flag.Uint flag.Uint64 flag.Bool flag.Float64 flag.Duration flag.StringVar flag.IntVar flag.Int64Var flag.UintVar flag.Uint64Var flag.BoolVar flag.Float64Var flag.DurationVar flag.Var flag.Func flag.BoolFunc flag.TextVar log.SetOutput log.SetFlags log.SetPrefix log/slog.SetDefault log/slog.SetLogLoggerLevel runtime/debug.SetGCPercent runtime/debug.SetMemoryLimit runtime/debug.SetMaxThreads runtime/debug.SetMaxStack
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason Process-wide settings couple leaves that have no declared link.
  source Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md); Google Go Style Guide, Best Practices (https://google.github.io/styleguide/go/best-practices)

# A library name is not `util`, `common`, `misc`, `helpers`, `shared`, or `base`.
rule ARCH-21
  kind declaration
  level error
  at library
  deny-names util common misc helpers shared base
  reason Such a name tells the reader nothing, and the package collects unrelated code and dependencies.
  source Go Blog, Package names (https://go.dev/blog/package-names)

# Code does not drop an `error` result.
rule ERR-01
  kind code-form
  level error
  form dropped-error
  deferred-ok (*database/sql.Tx).Rollback (*database/sql.Rows).Close (*database/sql.Stmt).Close (*database/sql.Conn).Close (*os.File).Close (io.Closer).Close
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason A dropped error hides a failure.
  source Go Wiki, Go Code Review Comments (https://go.dev/wiki/CodeReviewComments); golangci-lint, Linters (https://golangci-lint.run/docs/linters/); gosec rule list (RULES.md) (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/securego/gosec/master/RULES.md); Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md)

# Each `_ = f()` that discards an error has a comment that gives the reason.
rule ERR-03
  kind code-form
  level error
  form discard-error
  unless-comment yes
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason A deliberate discard must be visible and defended.
  source Go Wiki, Go Code Review Comments (https://go.dev/wiki/CodeReviewComments); Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md); gosec README (https://github.com/securego/gosec)

# Code compares errors with `errors.Is` or `errors.As`, not with `==`, a type assertion, or the error text.
rule ERR-04
  kind code-form
  level error
  form error-compare
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason A direct comparison fails on a wrapped error, and the text is not an API.
  source Go Blog, Working with Errors in Go 1.13 (https://go.dev/blog/go1.13-errors); golangci-lint, Linters (https://golangci-lint.run/docs/linters/); Google Go Style Guide, Best Practices (https://google.github.io/styleguide/go/best-practices)

# Leaf code and library code do not call `os.Exit`, `log.Fatal`, or `log.Panic` functions.
rule ERR-08
  kind forbid-call
  level error
  funcs os.Exit log.Fatal log.Fatalf log.Fatalln log.Panic log.Panicf log.Panicln (*log.Logger).Fatal* (*log.Logger).Panic*
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason Only `main` may end the process, and `main` is generated here.
  source Uber Go Style Guide (https://github.com/uber-go/guide/blob/master/style.md); Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md)

# Each type assertion uses the two-value form.
rule ERR-09
  kind code-form
  level error
  form one-value-assertion
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason A failed one-value assertion panics.
  source Uber Go Style Guide (https://github.com/uber-go/guide/blob/master/style.md); golangci-lint, Linters (https://golangci-lint.run/docs/linters/)

# Error strings start with a lower-case letter and do not end with punctuation.
rule ERR-13
  kind call-form
  level error
  funcs errors.New fmt.Errorf
  require-text ^[a-z] [^.:!?\n]$
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason Callers append context to errors.
  source Go Wiki, Go Code Review Comments (https://go.dev/wiki/CodeReviewComments); Staticcheck, Checks (https://staticcheck.dev/docs/checks/)

# A function that takes a `context.Context` takes it as the first parameter, named `ctx`.
rule CTX-01
  kind declaration
  level error
  at param
  types context.Context
  require first name=ctx
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason One form makes context flow easy to read and to check.
  source Go standard library, package context (https://pkg.go.dev/context)

# A struct does not have a `context.Context` field.
rule CTX-02
  kind declaration
  level error
  at field
  deny-types context.Context
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason A stored context hides its lifetime.
  source Go standard library, package context (https://pkg.go.dev/context); Go Wiki, Go Code Review Comments (https://go.dev/wiki/CodeReviewComments)

# Code does not pass a nil `context.Context`.
rule CTX-03
  kind call-form
  level error
  param-type context.Context
  require not-nil
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason A callee may dereference it.
  source Go standard library, package context (https://pkg.go.dev/context); Staticcheck, Checks (https://staticcheck.dev/docs/checks/)

# Code uses the context forms of calls that can block: `http.NewRequestWithContext`, `QueryContext`, `ExecContext`, `BeginTx`, `DialContext`, `exec.CommandContext`.
rule CTX-06
  kind forbid-call
  level error
  funcs net/http.NewRequest net/http.Get net/http.Head net/http.Post net/http.PostForm (*net/http.Client).Get (*net/http.Client).Head (*net/http.Client).Post (*net/http.Client).PostForm (*database/sql.DB).Query (*database/sql.DB).QueryRow (*database/sql.DB).Exec (*database/sql.DB).Begin (*database/sql.DB).Prepare (*database/sql.DB).Ping (*database/sql.Tx).Query (*database/sql.Tx).QueryRow (*database/sql.Tx).Exec (*database/sql.Tx).Prepare (*database/sql.Stmt).Query (*database/sql.Stmt).QueryRow (*database/sql.Stmt).Exec net.Dial net.DialTimeout (*net.Dialer).Dial crypto/tls.Dial (*crypto/tls.Dialer).Dial os/exec.Command
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason A call without a context cannot stop when its caller stops.
  source golangci-lint, Linters (https://golangci-lint.run/docs/linters/); Go documentation, Canceling in-progress database operations (https://go.dev/doc/database/cancel-operations); Go standard library, package database/sql (https://pkg.go.dev/database/sql)

# Context values use an unexported key type and hold only request-scoped data, not optional parameters.
rule CTX-07
  kind call-form
  level error
  funcs context.WithValue
  arg 1
  require unexported-type
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason A hidden parameter breaks the visible signature.
  source Go standard library, package context (https://pkg.go.dev/context); Staticcheck, Checks (https://staticcheck.dev/docs/checks/)

# A port method whose provider reaches a network or acquiring function takes `context.Context` as its first parameter.
rule CTX-08
  kind declaration
  level error
  at wired-port
  to gateway
  reason A deadline cannot pass through a port that has no context.
  source Go standard library, package context (https://pkg.go.dev/context); Google SRE Book, Addressing Cascading Failures (https://sre.google/sre-book/addressing-cascading-failures/)

# An entry leaf serves through an `http.Server` with `ReadHeaderTimeout`, `ReadTimeout`, `WriteTimeout`, and `IdleTimeout` set, and does not call `http.ListenAndServe`, `http.ListenAndServeTLS`, or `http.Serve`.
rule HTTP-01
  kind forbid-call
  level error
  funcs net/http.ListenAndServe net/http.ListenAndServeTLS net/http.Serve
  in entry
  reason The package-level functions run with no timeouts, so a slow client can hold resources.
  source Cloudflare Blog, The complete guide to Go net/http timeouts (https://blog.cloudflare.com/the-complete-guide-to-golang-net-http-timeouts/); gosec rule list (RULES.md) (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/securego/gosec/master/RULES.md); Go standard library, package net/http (https://pkg.go.dev/net/http)

# An entry leaf serves through an `http.Server` with `ReadHeaderTimeout`, `ReadTimeout`, `WriteTimeout`, and `IdleTimeout` set, and does not call `http.ListenAndServe`, `http.ListenAndServeTLS`, or `http.Serve`.
rule HTTP-01.timeouts
  kind literal
  level error
  type net/http.Server
  require ReadHeaderTimeout ReadTimeout WriteTimeout IdleTimeout
  in entry
  reason The package-level functions run with no timeouts, so a slow client can hold resources.
  source Cloudflare Blog, The complete guide to Go net/http timeouts (https://blog.cloudflare.com/the-complete-guide-to-golang-net-http-timeouts/); gosec rule list (RULES.md) (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/securego/gosec/master/RULES.md); Go standard library, package net/http (https://pkg.go.dev/net/http)

# A gateway uses an `http.Client` with a non-zero `Timeout`, and does not call `http.Get`, `http.Post`, `http.Head`, `http.PostForm`, or `http.DefaultClient`.
rule HTTP-02
  kind forbid-call
  level error
  funcs net/http.Get net/http.Post net/http.Head net/http.PostForm net/http.DefaultClient
  in gateway
  reason `DefaultClient` has no timeout, so a stuck peer holds a goroutine.
  source Cloudflare Blog, The complete guide to Go net/http timeouts (https://blog.cloudflare.com/the-complete-guide-to-golang-net-http-timeouts/); Go standard library, package net/http (https://pkg.go.dev/net/http)

# A gateway uses an `http.Client` with a non-zero `Timeout`, and does not call `http.Get`, `http.Post`, `http.Head`, `http.PostForm`, or `http.DefaultClient`.
rule HTTP-02.timeout
  kind literal
  level error
  type net/http.Client
  require Timeout
  in gateway
  reason `DefaultClient` has no timeout, so a stuck peer holds a goroutine.
  source Cloudflare Blog, The complete guide to Go net/http timeouts (https://blog.cloudflare.com/the-complete-guide-to-golang-net-http-timeouts/); Go standard library, package net/http (https://pkg.go.dev/net/http)

# An entry leaf registers routes on its own `http.ServeMux`, not on `http.DefaultServeMux`.
rule HTTP-07
  kind forbid-call
  level error
  funcs net/http.Handle net/http.HandleFunc net/http.DefaultServeMux
  in entry
  reason Any imported package can add a route to the default mux.
  source Go standard library, package net/http (https://pkg.go.dev/net/http); Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md); gosec rule list (RULES.md) (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/securego/gosec/master/RULES.md)

# A gateway does not follow a redirect automatically, unless it checks the target against an allow-list.
rule HTTP-09
  kind literal
  level error
  type net/http.Client
  require CheckRedirect
  in gateway
  reason A redirect can move a permitted request to an internal target.
  source OWASP API10:2023 Unsafe Consumption of APIs (https://api-security.owasp.org/editions/2023/en/0xaa-unsafe-consumption-of-apis); OWASP Server Side Request Forgery Prevention Cheat Sheet (https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Server_Side_Request_Forgery_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)

# Code does not set `InsecureSkipVerify: true` or a `MinVersion` below TLS 1.2, except in test files.
rule HTTP-11
  kind literal
  level error
  type crypto/tls.Config
  deny InsecureSkipVerify=true
  below MinVersion=771
  in leaf gateway entry library
  files code
  reason Without verification, TLS does not stop a man in the middle.
  source Go standard library, package crypto/tls (https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/tls); gosec rule list (RULES.md) (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/securego/gosec/master/RULES.md); Stripe documentation, Integration security guide (https://docs.stripe.com/security/guide)

# Each entry route accepts only the methods that it lists, and answers others with 405.
rule HTTP-13
  kind call-form
  level error
  funcs (*net/http.ServeMux).Handle (*net/http.ServeMux).HandleFunc
  require constant
  require-text ^(GET|POST|PUT|PATCH|DELETE|HEAD|OPTIONS)\s
  in entry
  reason Unplanned methods widen the attack surface.
  source OWASP REST Security Cheat Sheet (https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/REST_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html); OWASP API8:2023 Security Misconfiguration (https://api-security.owasp.org/editions/2023/en/0xa8-security-misconfiguration)

# Each session cookie sets `Secure`, `HttpOnly`, and `SameSite` with the value `Strict` or `Lax`.
rule HTTP-17
  kind literal
  level error
  type net/http.Cookie
  require Secure=true HttpOnly=true SameSite=2,3
  in entry
  reason These attributes limit theft and cross-site use.
  source OWASP Session Management Cheat Sheet (https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Session_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html)

# Source files, declaration files, and test fixtures hold no real secret, key, or password.
rule SEC-01
  kind literal
  level error
  deny-text (sk_live_|sk_test_|AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}|ghp_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}|-----BEGIN[A-Z\s]*PRIVATE\sKEY)
  names *password* *Password* *secret* *Secret* *apiKey* *ApiKey* *APIKey* *token* *Token*
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason Anyone who reads the repository gets the secret, and history keeps it.
  source gosec rule list (RULES.md) (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/securego/gosec/master/RULES.md); Stripe documentation, Best practices for managing secret API keys (https://docs.stripe.com/keys-best-practices); OWASP Secrets Management Cheat Sheet (https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Secrets_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html); OWASP Cryptographic Storage Cheat Sheet (https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cryptographic_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html)

# A settings field that holds a credential has the tag `vulcan:"secret"`.
rule SEC-02
  kind declaration
  level error
  at settings-field
  names *Key *Token *Password *Secret *Credential *Credentials
  require vulcan=secret
  in leaf gateway entry
  reason The tag makes a literal value a compile error.
  source Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md)

# A SQL statement is a constant string, and each value goes in as a parameter.
rule SEC-07
  kind call-form
  level error
  funcs (*database/sql.DB).Query (*database/sql.DB).QueryRow (*database/sql.DB).Exec (*database/sql.DB).Prepare (*database/sql.DB).QueryContext (*database/sql.DB).QueryRowContext (*database/sql.DB).ExecContext (*database/sql.DB).PrepareContext (*database/sql.Tx).Query (*database/sql.Tx).QueryRow (*database/sql.Tx).Exec (*database/sql.Tx).Prepare (*database/sql.Tx).QueryContext (*database/sql.Tx).QueryRowContext (*database/sql.Tx).ExecContext (*database/sql.Tx).PrepareContext (*database/sql.Conn).QueryContext (*database/sql.Conn).QueryRowContext (*database/sql.Conn).ExecContext (*database/sql.Conn).PrepareContext
  require constant
  unless-comment yes
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason A built statement is a SQL injection risk.
  source Go documentation, Avoiding SQL injection risk (https://go.dev/doc/database/sql-injection); OWASP SQL Injection Prevention Cheat Sheet (https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/SQL_Injection_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html); gosec rule list (RULES.md) (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/securego/gosec/master/RULES.md)

# Security code does not use MD5, SHA-1, DES, or RC4.
rule SEC-10
  kind depends
  level error
  from leaf gateway entry library
  packages crypto/md5 crypto/sha1 crypto/des crypto/rc4
  reason These algorithms are broken.
  source gosec rule list (RULES.md) (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/securego/gosec/master/RULES.md); OWASP Cryptographic Storage Cheat Sheet (https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cryptographic_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html)

# Leaf code and library code do not import `unsafe` or `syscall`, do not use cgo, and do not call `reflect.Value.Call` or `reflect.Value.Method`.
rule SEC-30.imports
  kind depends
  level error
  from leaf gateway entry library
  packages unsafe syscall C
  reason These paths escape each static check.
  source Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md); gosec rule list (RULES.md) (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/securego/gosec/master/RULES.md)

# Leaf code and library code do not import `unsafe` or `syscall`, do not use cgo, and do not call `reflect.Value.Call` or `reflect.Value.Method`.
rule SEC-30.calls
  kind forbid-call
  level error
  funcs (reflect.Value).Call (reflect.Value).CallSlice (reflect.Value).Method (reflect.Value).MethodByName
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason These paths escape each static check.
  source Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md); gosec rule list (RULES.md) (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/securego/gosec/master/RULES.md)

# An entry leaf or a gateway does not decode outside data with `encoding/gob`.
rule SEC-31
  kind forbid-call
  level error
  funcs encoding/gob.NewDecoder
  in entry gateway
  reason Native serial formats do not suit untrusted data.
  source OWASP Deserialization Cheat Sheet (https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Deserialization_Cheat_Sheet.html)

# SQL text does not hold `BEGIN`, `COMMIT`, or `ROLLBACK`.
rule DATA-03
  kind call-form
  level error
  funcs (*database/sql.DB).Query (*database/sql.DB).QueryRow (*database/sql.DB).Exec (*database/sql.DB).Prepare (*database/sql.DB).QueryContext (*database/sql.DB).QueryRowContext (*database/sql.DB).ExecContext (*database/sql.DB).PrepareContext (*database/sql.Tx).Query (*database/sql.Tx).QueryRow (*database/sql.Tx).Exec (*database/sql.Tx).Prepare (*database/sql.Tx).QueryContext (*database/sql.Tx).QueryRowContext (*database/sql.Tx).ExecContext (*database/sql.Tx).PrepareContext (*database/sql.Conn).QueryContext (*database/sql.Conn).QueryRowContext (*database/sql.Conn).ExecContext (*database/sql.Conn).PrepareContext
  deny-text (?i)\b(BEGIN|COMMIT|ROLLBACK)\b
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason Manual statements can leave the database in an unpredictable state.
  source Go documentation, Executing transactions (https://go.dev/doc/database/execute-transactions)

# Code uses `time.Time` for instants and `time.Duration` for periods, not integers or strings.
rule DATA-14
  kind declaration
  level error
  at field param var
  names *At *Time *Timeout *Deadline *Duration *Interval *TTL *Delay at time timeout deadline duration interval ttl delay
  deny-types string int int8 int16 int32 int64 uint uint8 uint16 uint32 uint64 float32 float64
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason A bare number has no unit, and a mistake compiles.
  source Uber Go Style Guide (https://github.com/uber-go/guide/blob/master/style.md); Google AIP-142, Time and duration (https://google.aip.dev/142); golangci-lint, Linters (https://golangci-lint.run/docs/linters/)

# A plain leaf or a library does not call `time.Now` for a business decision, and takes time through a port.
rule DATA-15
  kind forbid-call
  level error
  funcs time.Now time.Since time.Until
  in leaf library
  files code
  reason A test must control the clock.
  source Martin Fowler, Eradicating Non-Determinism in Tests (https://martinfowler.com/articles/nonDeterminism.html); Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md)

# A money amount is an integer in the currency's smallest unit, or an exact decimal, and is never `float32` or `float64`.
rule PAY-01
  kind declaration
  level error
  at field param var
  names *Amount* *amount* *Price* *price* *Total* *total* *Cost* *cost* *Charge* *charge* *Refund* *refund* *Fee* *fee* *Balance* *balance* *Money* *money* *Cents* *cents*
  deny-types float32 float64
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason Binary floats do not add up exactly.
  source Stripe documentation, Supported currencies (https://docs.stripe.com/currencies); The Floating-Point Guide, Exact Types (https://floating-point-gui.de/formats/exact/); Martin Fowler, Money (PoEAA catalog) (https://martinfowler.com/eaaCatalog/money.html)

# A retry loop has a limit on attempts, exponential backoff, and jitter.
rule RES-02
  kind code-form
  level error
  form retry-loop
  in leaf gateway
  reason Unlimited or synchronized retries deepen an overload.
  source Google SRE Book, Addressing Cascading Failures (https://sre.google/sre-book/addressing-cascading-failures/); AWS Builders' Library, Timeouts, retries, and backoff with jitter (https://builder.aws.com/content/3EumjoZascWd1oZiEgL8ORlv3qE/timeouts-retries-and-backoff-with-jitter)

# A channel is unbuffered or has size one, unless a comment defends a larger size.
rule CONC-03
  kind code-form
  level warn
  form channel-size
  unless-comment yes
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason A large buffer hides a capacity decision.
  source Uber Go Style Guide (https://github.com/uber-go/guide/blob/master/style.md)

# Leaf code and library code log through `log/slog`, not through `log` or `fmt.Print` functions.
rule OBS-01
  kind forbid-call
  level error
  funcs log.* (*log.Logger).* fmt.Print fmt.Printf fmt.Println
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason Structured records are machine-readable and resist log injection.
  source Go standard library, package log/slog (https://pkg.go.dev/log/slog); OWASP Logging Cheat Sheet (https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Logging_Cheat_Sheet.html); golangci-lint, Linters (https://golangci-lint.run/docs/linters/)

# A log message text is constant, and variable data goes in attributes.
rule OBS-02
  kind call-form
  level error
  funcs log/slog.Debug log/slog.Info log/slog.Warn log/slog.Error log/slog.DebugContext log/slog.InfoContext log/slog.WarnContext log/slog.ErrorContext log/slog.Log (*log/slog.Logger).Debug (*log/slog.Logger).Info (*log/slog.Logger).Warn (*log/slog.Logger).Error (*log/slog.Logger).DebugContext (*log/slog.Logger).InfoContext (*log/slog.Logger).WarnContext (*log/slog.Logger).ErrorContext (*log/slog.Logger).Log
  require constant
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason Untrusted text in a message can forge lines.
  source OWASP Logging Cheat Sheet (https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Logging_Cheat_Sheet.html); gosec README (https://github.com/securego/gosec)

# A production build exposes no debug or profiling route, and each old API version has an owner and an end date.
rule API-04
  kind depends
  level error
  from leaf gateway entry library
  packages net/http/pprof expvar
  reason Forgotten endpoints are an attack surface.
  source OWASP API9:2023 Improper Inventory Management (https://api-security.owasp.org/editions/2023/en/0xa9-improper-inventory-management); gosec rule list (RULES.md) (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/securego/gosec/master/RULES.md)

# A port method that changes state declares a `requires` for the limits of its arguments.
rule CON-01
  kind declaration
  level error
  at port-method
  require requires
  except-names Get* List* Find* Read* Is* Has* Count* Load* Lookup* Exists*
  in leaf gateway entry
  reason A boundary is the best place to state what a caller must meet.
  source Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md)

# A `return` in a function with `ensures` does not itself cause an effect, such as `return tx.Commit()`.
rule CON-03
  kind code-form
  level warn
  form return-effect
  funcs (*database/sql.Tx).Commit (*database/sql.Tx).Exec (*database/sql.Tx).ExecContext (*database/sql.DB).Exec (*database/sql.DB).ExecContext (*net/http.Client).Do (*net/http.Client).Post (*net/http.Client).Get net/smtp.SendMail os.WriteFile os.Remove
  unless-comment yes
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason Go runs the effect first, and the check then fires too late.
  source Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md)

# Each suppression of a check names the check and gives a reason.
rule CODE-02
  kind code-form
  level error
  form suppression
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason An unexplained suppression hides a defect.
  source golangci-lint, Linters (https://golangci-lint.run/docs/linters/)

# A function above a set complexity gets a warning.
rule CODE-03
  kind code-form
  level warn
  form function-complexity
  limit 15
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason Complex functions are hard to review.
  source golangci-lint, Linters (https://golangci-lint.run/docs/linters/)

# A `switch` over a named constant set covers each value, or has a `default` with a reason.
rule CODE-04
  kind code-form
  level error
  form switch-exhaustive
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason A new state must not fall through quietly.
  source golangci-lint, Linters (https://golangci-lint.run/docs/linters/)

# A struct that code marshals has a field tag on each marshaled field.
rule CODE-05.json
  kind call-form
  level error
  funcs encoding/json.Marshal encoding/json.MarshalIndent (*encoding/json.Encoder).Encode
  arg 0
  require tagged=json
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason A rename must not change the wire format.
  source Uber Go Style Guide (https://github.com/uber-go/guide/blob/master/style.md); golangci-lint, Linters (https://golangci-lint.run/docs/linters/)

# A struct that code marshals has a field tag on each marshaled field.
rule CODE-05.xml
  kind call-form
  level error
  funcs encoding/xml.Marshal encoding/xml.MarshalIndent (*encoding/xml.Encoder).Encode
  arg 0
  require tagged=xml
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason A rename must not change the wire format.
  source Uber Go Style Guide (https://github.com/uber-go/guide/blob/master/style.md); golangci-lint, Linters (https://golangci-lint.run/docs/linters/)

# An exported struct in a library does not embed another type.
rule CODE-06
  kind declaration
  level error
  at embedded
  in library
  reason Embedding leaks methods into the API.
  source Uber Go Style Guide (https://github.com/uber-go/guide/blob/master/style.md)

# Each port, topic, `external`, library, and exported name has a doc comment.
rule CODE-08
  kind declaration
  level error
  at doc
  in leaf gateway entry library
  files code
  reason Diagrams and generated docs read these comments.
  source Go Wiki, Go Code Review Comments (https://go.dev/wiki/CodeReviewComments); Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md)

# Near-duplicate functions become one function, in the leaf or in a library.
rule CODE-09
  kind code-form
  level error
  form duplicate-function
  limit 60
  similarity 90
  in leaf gateway entry library
  files code
  reason Duplicate code diverges, and models write much of it.
  source Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md)

# Code does not use a deprecated function, and has no unused name.
rule CODE-11.deprecated
  kind code-form
  level error
  form deprecated-use
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason Deprecated code loses support, and dead code misleads a reader.
  source Staticcheck, Checks (https://staticcheck.dev/docs/checks/); golangci-lint, Linters (https://golangci-lint.run/docs/linters/); Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md)

# Code does not use a deprecated function, and has no unused name.
rule CODE-11.unused
  kind code-form
  level error
  form unused-name
  in leaf gateway entry library
  reason Deprecated code loses support, and dead code misleads a reader.
  source Staticcheck, Checks (https://staticcheck.dev/docs/checks/); golangci-lint, Linters (https://golangci-lint.run/docs/linters/); Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md)

# A test body has no branch or loop, apart from a loop over a table of cases.
rule TEST-04
  kind code-form
  level error
  form test-logic
  reason A test must be plainly correct on reading.
  source Software Engineering at Google, Chapter 12, Unit Testing (https://abseil.io/resources/swe-book/html/ch12.html); Go Wiki, Table Driven Tests (https://go.dev/wiki/TableDrivenTests)

# A test does not call `time.Sleep`.
rule TEST-05
  kind forbid-call
  level error
  funcs time.Sleep
  files test
  reason A sleep wastes time or fails on a slow host.
  source Martin Fowler, Eradicating Non-Determinism in Tests (https://martinfowler.com/articles/nonDeterminism.html); Go standard library, package testing/synctest (https://pkg.go.dev/testing/synctest)

# Each deployment-specific value comes from a flag or from the environment, and leaf code holds no address or hostname literal.
rule BLD-07
  kind literal
  level error
  deny-text ^(https?://|\d+\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+|localhost|[a-z0-9.-]+\.(com|net|org|io|dev|local|internal)(:\d+)?$|[a-z0-9.-]*:\d+$)
  in leaf gateway entry
  files code
  reason One build must run in each environment.
  source The Twelve-Factor App, Config (https://12factor.net/config); The Twelve-Factor App, Backing services (https://12factor.net/backing-services); Vulcan Language Specification, Draft 0 (input/spec.md)

rule DEP-LIBRARY
  kind depends
  level error
  from library
  deny leaf gateway entry
  via import
  reason A library depends on no leaf.
  source docs/poc/plan-r3.md, section 3

rule DEP-GATEWAY
  kind depends
  level error
  from gateway
  deny leaf gateway entry
  via wire
  reason A gateway calls no other leaf.
  source docs/poc/plan-r3.md, section 3

rule DEP-ENTRY
  kind depends
  level error
  from leaf gateway entry library
  deny entry
  via wire
  reason No part calls an entry leaf.
  source docs/poc/plan-r3.md, section 3

rule DEP-LOCK
  kind depends
  level off
  map locked
  reason A new dependency fails until rules.lock changes; off by the owner's decision 1 of plan-r3, section 8.
  source docs/poc/plan-r3.md, section 3
